# 5g — Comprar. Sized XL and split THREE ways on 2026-09-24, on the day it was
# taken and before a line of it was written. THE ROW SAID `M`. It named seven
# deliverables; the sizing found EIGHTEEN, and three of them were things the row
# did not say at all.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE SIZE IS THE WEAKEST OF THE THREE REASONS THIS SPLIT EXISTS, and it is
# named last on purpose — the working agreement was amended by the owner on
# 2026-09-24 so that an M or an L is one sitting, and a session reaching for a
# size argument at M is asking for the old rule back. All three of the
# agreement's surviving reasons apply here, independently:
#
#   1. A GATE. 5g-iii is blocked on a word the owner owes — what `Costos`
#      SHOWS — and 5g-i and 5g-ii are not. The 2026-09-22 ruling was "leave
#      Costos dead until 5g", which said WHEN and never WHAT; a session that
#      picked between "last price paid", "a per-provider comparison" and "a
#      trailing series" would be taking a decision on his behalf about a screen
#      §2.11 fences out of every suite here. This is 5f-i/5f-ii's arrangement
#      exactly, one split later.
#   2. TWO FAILURE CLASSES, AND ONE OF THEM IS INVISIBLE HERE. This is the
#      strong one and it was MEASURED on 2026-09-24 rather than argued:
#        * provider_select admits ANY member (my_workspaces(), 0002:522);
#        * provider_price_memory is MANAGER-AND-ABOVE, inherited from purchase
#          and purchase_line's own policies through security_invoker (0008);
#        * record_purchase fences NEITHER — it is security definer with the
#          location wall and no role check at all (0018:165).
#      So a cashier on Comprar sees a provider list that works, a price memory
#      that is ALWAYS EMPTY — 200 and an empty array, never a 403 — which
#      renders as §2.8's legitimate "new pairing, type a price" state and is
#      indistinguishable from it; she then records a delivery that SUCCEEDS and
#      can never read it back. Every symptom of the broken case is a designed
#      state of the working one. Nothing on the screen can tell them apart, and
#      nothing on the screen is the instrument for either.
#   3. AND THEN SIZE. Comprar is Vender plus four things Vender does not have: a
#      provider in the header, an editable price per line, three price states
#      that must look different, and a commit that BLOCKS. Vender is
#      app/src/app/(tabs)/vender.tsx at 1,792 lines and took four sessions
#      (5f-i, 5f-ii, 5f-iii-a, 5f-iii-b). Eighteen deliverables over a new API
#      module, a live contract check, a change to two shipped modules and the
#      largest screen in the app is not one sitting by any reading.
#
# THREE THINGS WERE NOT IN THE PARENT ROW WHEN IT WAS TAKEN, and that is most of
# what the sizing was worth. All three are now IN the parent row, which is what
# assertion 3 needs to stay non-vacuous.
#   * THE PURCHASE PAYLOAD HAS NO PROVIDER IN IT. draftOf builds
#     {location_id, lines}; record_purchase raises 22023 — "a delivery has a
#     counterparty" — on a null p_provider_id (0018:200). So the buy side of a
#     module that already SHIPPED cannot commit at all, and the row read as
#     though Comprar were only a screen.
#   * A TYPED PURCHASE PRICE HAS NOWHERE TO LIVE. C3.13 makes the purchase price
#     something a person enters, and Quotes is the map 5f-i built for exactly
#     this and left empty. §2.11 persists the cart because a basket that does
#     not survive a phone ringing is a shopkeeper re-keying in front of a
#     customer — and the figures on a delivery note are worse to re-key than a
#     basket, because she has to find the note again.
#   * THE PREFILL IS STORED PER BASE AND READ PER PRICE UNIT.
#     provider_price_memory.unit_price_net_per_base is a numeric(14,6) per BASE
#     unit; the shopkeeper reads $8.50 / kg. And last_qty_display_unit is the
#     denomination she typed LAST TIME, which need not be the variant's
#     price_unit_code today. That is arithmetic, and it is nowhere in app/ yet.
#
# ⚠️ AND ONE MEASUREMENT THAT IS NOT A DELIVERABLE, RECORDED HERE SO IT IS NOT
# RE-DISCOVERED: unit_price_net_per_base comes off the wire as a JSON NUMBER
# (0.018000), which is a double, and @tienda/money's parseDecimal refuses a
# number argument outright. The read must cast ::text, exactly as
# app/src/api/catalog.ts's PRICE_COLUMNS already does. Measured against a real
# PostgREST on 2026-09-24; assertion 4 of 5d-i's check makes the same claim one
# table over and is the precedent.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT THIS SPLIT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT COVER, named so no session reads it
# as a gap: the `Genérico` seed. F6 requires a provider named Genérico in every
# workspace; the applied schema has seeded one since 0002 and it is named
# `Compra directa` — verified live on 2026-09-24, and carried forward unchanged
# through 0027 and 0034. THE ROW EXISTS, so F6's substance is satisfied and no
# child owns it; what differs is a STRING a shopkeeper reads in the header. It
# is parked as a decision rather than assigned, because renaming it after a
# shop holds deliveries is a fix-forward migration plus an UPDATE, and choosing
# it now is free.
#
# ⚠️ THIS GUARDS NO MIGRATION, and EACH_CHILD_SAYS asserts it POSITIVELY in all
# three rows because merging is automated: a child that quietly grows one is
# repaired by a fix-forward migration, never by an edit. It was measured rather
# than hoped — provider, provider_price_memory, purchase, purchase_line and
# record_purchase are all applied and all carry what these three children need.
# ⚠️ AND IT IS THE THING THE `Genérico` RULING WOULD CHANGE, which is exactly
# why that question is parked in front of this split rather than inside it.
SPLIT_ID="5g"
SPLIT_GROUPS=( "5g|5g-i 5g-ii 5g-iii" )
DELIVERABLES=(
  # ⚠️ ONE SPELLING PER ROW, and never an alternation: a bare pipe in the regex
  # field truncates the entry and it fails downstream as a DROPPED deliverable,
  # which reads exactly like the defect this list exists to catch.
  #
  # ⚠️ NO BACKTICKS IN A REGEX. This file is SOURCED by bash, so a backtick is
  # command substitution. Match the words INSIDE the backticks instead.
  #
  # ⚠️ EVERY REGEX MUST ALSO MATCH THE PARENT ROW — assertion 3 refuses a
  # deliverable the parent stopped promising.
  "the provider directory as something a screen can choose from|provider list read|5g-i"
  "the last price paid TO THAT PROVIDER, and never another one's|provider_price_memory|5g-i"
  "the prefill is stored per base and a shopkeeper reads it per price unit|per PRICE UNIT|5g-i"
  "the denomination she typed last time, which may not be today's|last_qty_display_unit|5g-i"
  "the provider on the payload, without which a purchase cannot commit|p_provider_id|5g-i"
  "a purchase price is entered, and the basket it lives in is persisted|typed price, persisted with the basket|5g-i"
  "the first thing in this repository ever to call record_purchase|the live round trip|5g-i"
  "what a cashier can read, write and never see again|cashier asymmetry|5g-i"
  "the provider chosen first, in the header|Comprando a|5g-ii"
  "C3.11's other half — the basket is re-priced when the provider changes|re-prices every row|5g-ii"
  "§2.8's three states, and the middle one visibly not a prefill|three price states|5g-ii"
  "no memory is a dash and never a zero|C3\\.12|5g-ii"
  "a purchase cannot be committed while any row has no price|C3\\.13|5g-ii"
  "and the missing price is set from where she already is|fast from where|5g-ii"
  "the sheet, the slide and the two confirmations|the shape 5f-iii shipped|5g-ii"
  "no 50-centavo rounding on the buy side|C12\\.3|5g-ii"
  "the word deferred onto this row on 2026-09-22|what Costos shows|5g-iii"
  "the button that has been visible and dead since 5d-iii|drew dead on La Familia|5g-iii"
)
PHRASES=(
  "5g-i|F|NO SCREEN|The 5f-i, 5e-i, 5d-i and 5d-iv-a shape, for the reason all four gave: everything in this child has a right answer a suite or a live check can read, and putting it in the same row as a screen means the half nothing can see is reviewed as though somebody had looked at it."
  "5g-i|F|never across providers|§2.8 and C3.11. A supplier price is a fact about a relationship, not about a product — so a memory learned from one provider must never prefill another's. The ADR says why in terms a screen cannot restate: the operator would ACCEPT a borrowed prefill, because it looks exactly like the case where the system knows."
  "5g-i|F|live round trip|record_purchase has been applied since 0018 and nothing in app/ has ever sent it anything. A node suite reads the payload's shape; only real HTTP against a reset database reads whether Postgres accepts it. 5f-i's row named this task as the one that owes it."
  "5g-i|F|cashier asymmetry|Measured on 2026-09-24, not inferred. provider_select admits any member; provider_price_memory is manager-and-above through security_invoker; record_purchase fences neither. The failure is invisible because the broken case renders as §2.8's designed empty state — which is the whole argument for this child being its own row."
  "5g-i|F|ships no migration|A POSITIVE assertion because merging is automated: a child that quietly grew a migration is repaired only by a fix-forward migration, never by an edit. Every table and function this child reads has been applied since 0018 at the latest."
  "5g-ii|I|owner's phone is the whole instrument|R9 and §2.11. Every judgement left in this child is rendering, navigation or layout, and no check here will ever say it is wrong. A row that does not say so reads like a row something is watching."
  "5g-ii|F|empty and required|§2.8's middle price state, and the one that matters. You have bought this product, but never from THIS provider: it must be visibly distinct from a prefill, because an empty required field asks a question and a wrong prefill answers one nobody asked."
  "5g-ii|F|BLOCKED|C3.13, and it is the owner's own rule read against C3.14: a SALE at a missing price goes through loudly, a PURCHASE does not go through at all. One basket, two answers, and 5f-i made them one number — Basket.complete — so the two screens cannot disagree about the same basket."
  "5g-ii|I|third drawing of a search box|§2.8 opens with three capture screens sharing one engine underneath, and 5f-ii's row already recorded the second drawing as the pattern 5h.5 extracts. src/ui/ is built across 5d–5h; 5h.5 writes its conventions AFTER. A third copy-paste is how that sentence quietly stops being true."
  "5g-iii|F|GATED|The 2026-09-22 ruling was leave Costos dead until 5g. It said WHEN and never WHAT, so the word is still owed. Last price paid, a per-provider comparison and a trailing series are three different screens over the same rows, and §2.11 fences all three out of every suite here — so a session picking between them is deciding on the owner's behalf with no instrument."
  "5g-iii|F|not Comprar|familia/[id].tsx is where the dead button is. This child opens a file the other two never touch, which is the cheapest possible check that the split's seam is real rather than administrative."
)
EACH_CHILD_SAYS=(
  "I|ships no migration|provider (0002), provider_price_memory (0008), purchase and purchase_line (0003) and record_purchase (0018) are all applied and all carry what these three children need — measured, not assumed. A POSITIVE assertion because merging is automated. ⚠️ AND IT IS WHAT THE Genérico RULING WOULD CHANGE: renaming the seeded generic provider is a fix-forward migration plus an UPDATE of live rows, which is why that question is parked in front of this split rather than inside it."
)
